teeproxy includes the independent Rust attestation client developed alongside
teerouter, adapted into a loopback API gateway with verified TLS connection
pooling, bounded streaming and agent base-URL configuration.

The inherited MIT notice is retained in LICENSE. The teellm protocol domain and
attestation endpoint names are retained for wire compatibility with teerouter.
No management platform, browser UI or router server implementation is included.

Intel TDX verification uses the pinned dcap-qvl dependency. Optional AMD SEV-SNP
verification uses sev and OpenSSL. Dependencies retain their own licenses.
Public verification fixtures retain source attribution and licenses under
tests/fixtures/tdx and tests/fixtures/snp. These historical fixtures are not
approved production policies.
